# No em dashes

Never use the em dash (`—`) in copy, marketing text, UI strings, blog posts, docs meant for readers, or any other prose.

Prefer:

- a colon for labels or introductions (`Photo placeholder: booth view`)
- a comma or period to break a sentence
- parentheses for asides

```text
❌ Quiet writing on immersive rehab — no marketing kit
✅ Quiet writing on immersive rehab: no marketing kit

❌ Crete — a keynote on interactive rehab
✅ Crete: a keynote on interactive rehab

❌ Institute — ranked top globally — the program
✅ Institute (ranked top globally), the program
```

En dashes in numeric ranges (`17-19` or `17–19`) are fine. Do not substitute an em dash for a hyphen, comma, colon, or parenthesis.
